From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: account pictures from Chromium itself, chosen in
 setup

ChromeOS's default account pictures are downloaded from Google's server
(gstatic.com), so offline an account shows the anonymous picture. Chromium
has 29 of them itself: the desktop browser's profile avatars
(chrome/app/theme/default_100_percent/common/modern_avatars: illustrations,
food and origami animals, 96 px), the same artwork under the same names.

- webui_theme_resources.grd builds them on ChromeOS too.
- default_user_images.cc: those 29 are the current set (kBundledImages maps
  each default image index to its IDR_PROFILE_AVATAR_N); their URLs are
  chrome://theme/IDR_PROFILE_AVATAR_N, the others' the anonymous picture's.
- UserImageManagerImpl loads a default picture from the resource pack, PNG
  bytes included, never from the network. An account whose picture
  Chromium does not have (given before) keeps the copy saved then.
- Personalization's avatar page shows chrome://theme URLs as they are and no
  longer needs to be online to show or pick them.
- Creating an account (LocalAccountCreationScreen) shows the picture it
  will get, a random one, and "Change" opens a grid of the 29. The choice
  waits in the local state pref nickel.setup.pending_avatars, by the
  account's email, until the account's first sign-in gives it its first
  picture (SetInitialUserImage), in whichever Chrome signs in first.
  A photo of one's own stays in Settings (Personalization), after setup.

